A bad or out-of-range max_auto_continues now prints a warning at startup instead of being dropped or clamped silently. Committed as 0ad8d9be, and the title says "Fixes #1030". Build, the full cargo test (6630 passed, 0 failed), clippy with -D warnings, and the fmt check all pass.

What changed
• The warning: a new function, config::max_auto_continues_warning, decides whether a value deserves one. Junk like "abc", "-1" or "" says the default cap of 5 applies, and anything above 20 says it's capped at 20. The value shown is passed through sanitize_for_display and cut at 64 bytes.
• Valid values stay silent: every in-range value, 0 through 20, gets no warning. That includes 0, which already means "auto-continue off" and which /config set accepts.
• Where it prints: in src/cli.rs, right after the cost_warn lines, with the same gating (one stderr line, not hidden by quiet mode). To reach the default from there I made `DEFAULT_MAX_AUTO_CONTINUES` in `src/repl.rs pub(crate)`.
• What didn't change: the parse, fallback and clamp logic, and the exit code.
• Why it only warns: the commit body gives the reason in the words you set out. The knob is a cap, both fallbacks have a limit, and the line prints before any token is spent.
• Docs: docs/src/usage/repl.md now gives the 0–20 range and mentions the warning.

Checks
• Built binary, run in an empty temp dir:
  • "abc" printed warning: invalid max_auto_continues value 'abc' (use a whole number from 0 to 20); the auto-continue cap uses the default (5)
  • 500 printed …; capped at 20
  • 5 printed nothing.
  • All three runs exited 1, but that's the later "No API key" stop, not this change.
• Tests: the bad values are checked against the full expected string, the valid values are checked to return nothing, and there's an escape-byte fixture whose input is confirmed to contain \x1b while the output doesn't.
• Positive control: forcing the function to always return nothing made the two tests that expect a warning fail by name, while the valid-values test stayed green. I put the code back in the same command; everything is green again and no NEUTERED marker is left.
• Close-out: I re-read #1030. A grep for silent .parse::<number>().ok() calls in the config readers finds only this one, so there was nothing new to file. That search covers only that one pattern.

The module-size gate now reports src/cli.rs at 24 lines over its recorded size. It's a non-fatal warning, and I didn't update the register.
